WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.910
Some love scenes transcend even circumstantial
weirdness, and are so painfully awkward in

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.349
and of themselves that you'd be embarrassed
to watch them alone, much less with other

00:00:08.349 --> 00:00:08.840
people.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.160
Luckily, the lovemaking experts here at Looper
are ready to help you steer around the trainwrecks

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.860
with this look at some love scenes that went
way too far.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.540
Gone Girl has a few grisly scenes, but the
one that takes the cake is undoubtedly the

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.539
scene where Amy brutally slaughters a hapless
love interest in order to frame her husband

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.180
for the crime.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.960
It's sickeningly violent, and far too disturbing
to actually show you, so instead, here's some

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.240
footage of a hospital patient being cuddled
back to life by adorable kittens.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.080
Trust us, it's for your own good.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.360
Second only to that blue naked guy, the weirdest
thing in Watchmen just might be the big love

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.860
scene between superheroes Nite Owl and Silk
Spectre.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.180
After trying once before and failing when
Nite Owl couldn't, uh, perform his superhero

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.300
duties, the duo went out and beat up a bunch
of crooks, which gave them the pizazz they

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.100
needed to do the deed.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.410
It's meant to be commentary on the kinky intersection
of violence and romance for people who dress

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.000
up in fetish gear to fight crime.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:02.780
But it's actually just offputting, especially
the choice to have Leonard Cohen's "Hallelujah"

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.040
as the scene's soundtrack.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.320
What the heck were they thinking?

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.400
The 40-Year-Old Virgin consists almost entirely
of one uncomfortable scene after another.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.460
It's about a bunch of boorish dudes who work
at an electronics store and decide to help

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.820
their nerdy colleague Andy nail down his first
intimate experience.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.170
That advice is disastrous, as shown clearly
in the aborted love scene between Andy and

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:26.390
Beth, an overly dominating hookup who nearly
initiates Andy into all sorts of things he's

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.460
not ready for, before his friends bail him
out.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.520
Close call for him and for the audience.

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:35.520
For The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn: Part
I, the filmmakers ran into trouble with the

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.749
long-awaited moment of physical intimacy between
the human Bella and the superpowered glitter

00:01:39.749 --> 00:01:40.780
vampire Edward.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.960
Star Kristen Stewart explained the resulting
mess to Harper's Bazaar UK, saying,

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.259
"It had to be transcendent and otherworldly,
inhuman, better sex than you can possibly

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:52.140
ever imagine, and we were like, 'How do we
live up to that?'

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.400
It was agony.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.500
Which sucks, because I wanted it to be so
good."

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.240
That's how we all felt about the entire series,
so you're in good company, Kristen.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.820
James Cameron's CGI world of Avatar was so
different, so alien, that even the act of

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:06.950
physical intimacy was something to behold.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.750
Of course, that doesn't take into consideration
whether or not it was something anyone actually

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:11.260
wanted to behold.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.680
Here's the main thing: on the planet Pandora,
making love is basically just plug and play.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:20.740
Thanks to his Na'vi avatar, human Marine Jake
Sully can get busy with actual Na'vi female

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.360
Neytiri.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.180
Of course, that means connecting the tendrils
on the ends of their braids to fully experience

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.900
one another in the most intimate of ways.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.610
And let's not forget, this all goes down in
a purple jellyfish forest.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.720
Thanks, James Cameron!

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.040
"I'm the King of the world."

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.440
The 2003 mega-flop Gigli is one of the most
renowned critical and box office turkeys of

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:38.960
all time.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:43.080
And a big part of that is the embarrassingly
squicky love scene between Ben Affleck and

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:43.980
Jennifer Lopez.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.260
"It's turkey time."

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:48.620
"huh?"

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.660
"Gobble gobble."

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.440
Rumor has it that the studio forced acclaimed
director Martin Brest to change the film in

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.730
order to showcase the real-life romance between
Lopez and Affleck.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.700
If so, that was a terrible idea.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.760
So bad, in fact, that Brest retired from filmmaking
entirely as a result.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.340
And after watching this love scene, we totally
get why.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.480
Howard the Duck is a lot of things.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.720
For instance, it was the first bomb of George
Lucas's career.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.460
And it's the only movie, or at least the only
mainstream American comedy, to feature a romantic

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.560
tryst between a female rock star and a man-sized,
anthropomorphic duck.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.820
"let's go for it, mister macho"

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.560
"It's just that you're so incredibly soft
and cuddly"

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.000
Howard has since been reintroduced in the
Marvel Cinematic Universe, but so far, there's

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.320
been no sign of any romance for Howard.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.080
Fingers crossed we never see this again.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.940
The 1993 sci-fi satire Demolition Man had
an ambitious and bizarre view of what "the

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:41.480
future" would be like.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:46.120
Sylvester Stallone's character John Spartan
wakes from a cryogenic freeze to find that

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.860
peace reigns, and also that people make love
using virtual reality helmets.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.640
What follows is a ridiculous scene where Sandra
Bullock's police lieutenant Huxley attempts

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.740
to seduce him in the clumsiest way possible,
including playing the theme from The Love

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:01.160
Boat as an aphrodisiac as weird images jolt
through his mind.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.440
Needless to say, Spartan is not amused or
aroused.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.340
"alright Huxley, what do you say we just do
it the old fashioned way?"

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.100
"ew, disgusting!!

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.720
You mean… fluid transfer?!"

